Backport the Anki security fixes shipped through 26.09.3 to 25.09.2.

Sources: https://github.com/ankitects/anki/compare/25.09.2...25.09.4
https://github.com/ankitects/anki/commit/b81c3b2cc497c32cba0f029afc8421d288a6630b
https://github.com/ankitects/anki/commit/71bd36ff074934c4bc0af56e2a5c2541da8a1b19
https://github.com/ankitects/anki/commit/6eb89c06488727f57f5c03f31e4ee3c30ee27737
https://github.com/ankitects/anki/commit/7add01b1bc89d81126b47b235ee24402159fce02
https://github.com/ankitects/anki/commit/83254832b0fbe00602b5a6381c78ae59ccaf6c25
https://github.com/ankitects/anki/commit/a39e1b7ee3b28b61bf07a40c66bab1315eff5889
https://github.com/ankitects/anki/blob/26.09.3/rslib/src/notetype/emptycards.rs

Adaptations: retain the legacy editor and route names, attach route metadata
without adding the newer editor, and guard the common image-menu entry point.
Enable upstream's SvelteKit bootstrap hashes for the untrusted occlusion route.
Retain the existing Cargo graph while updating rustls and rustls-webpki.

